Tracing the actual flow: _initiateWithdraw is reachable only for an account's own position, and only after
  require(PT.isExpired()). For an expired principal token, redemption is not a market swap at a discount/premium —
  _redeemPT takes the PT.isExpired() branch into PendlePTLib.redeemExpiredPT, which burns the PT and pulls the exact
  underlying entitlement out of the SY at the issuer's own redemption terms. The value received is therefore the
  realized value of exactly the ptAmount being withdrawn, not a lossy conversion.

  The critical point is what the two arguments to initiateWithdraw are for. yieldTokenAmount: tokenOutSy is the actual,
  measured quantity of the post-redemption token escrowed for this specific request; sharesAmount: sharesHeld is the
  share quantity being escrowed against that same request. The pair is a per-account tuple, not a price. The manager
  needs sharesAmount to split/prorate the same request when the position is partially finalized or transferred; it does
  not use it to convert one denomination into the other. Nothing in this function writes to a pooled
  yield-token-per-share accumulator, and nothing here changes the backing of shares held by other depositors: the
  redeemed PT are burned and the resulting proceeds are earmarked to the requesting account's escrowed shares. The other
  depositors' PT balance and their share count both remain untouched, so no ratio they own moves.

  The code comment states this is the deliberate design ("Since the vault shares are stored in PT terms, we pass
  tokenOutSy terms ... to the withdraw implementation"), and the claim's asserted harm — "the shortfall is socialised
  onto every other depositor" — depends entirely on accounting inside AbstractStakingStrategy and
  IWithdrawRequestManager, neither of which is presented. To hold, the claim would need the manager to treat
  yieldTokenAmount/sharesAmount as a pool-wide exchange rate applied to non-requesting holders; no such step is shown,
  and the visible flow is consistent with per-request escrow where a requester bears their own realized redemption
  outcome. The finding never identifies the exact line where an unchanged share supply is revalued against the pooled
  balance, which is the step the whole exploit rests on.

  Under the tie-break, an unverified cross-contract accounting assumption cannot carry a High.

  CONSTRAINT|class=C22|A denomination-mismatch claim must point to the concrete line where the mismatched quantity feeds
  a pooled, supply-wide valuation shared by non-acting participants; if the mismatched pair is only ever stored and
  prorated within the acting party's own earmarked request, the loss is self-inflicted, not socialised, and the claim
  fails.
  VERDICT|REFUTED|src/staking/PendlePT.sol:_initiateWithdraw:148|class=C22|The expired-PT branch redeems the caller's
  own ptAmount at the issuer's redemption terms and escrows the measured proceeds against that same account's sharesHeld
  as a per-request tuple — no shown code converts that pair into a pool-wide rate or alters any other depositor's PT
  backing or share count.
